(S, "A helicopter needs 50 gallons of fuel to travel 320 km. How many gallons does it need to travel 700 km?", ["109.375", "120", "100", "175"], 0, "Fuel per km is 50 / 320. For 700 km: 50 x 700 / 320 = 35000 / 320 = 109.375 gallons.", "This is a direct proportion: more distance needs more fuel in the same ratio.", [1945]),
